Be concise and direct.

Do not explain code unless asked.

This is a WordPress project. Follow WordPress coding patterns.

Do not introduce frameworks, build tools, or modern JS stacks unless requested.

Do not rewrite entire template files for small changes.

Modify only the necessary section of code.

Preserve existing HTML structure and CSS class names.

Do not rename ACF field names.

Do not change WordPress hooks, template hierarchy, or function signatures unless required.

Avoid adding comments unless logic is complex.

Keep PHP procedural if the existing codebase is procedural.

Do not add security, sanitization, or escaping functions unless requested.

For styling tasks, modify CSS only — do not touch PHP/HTML.

For ACF-related work:
- Use existing field names
- Do not add new fields unless asked
- Follow current field structure

Output no more than 120 lines of code.

Assume the developer understands WordPress, PHP, and CSS.
